2025-05-01 00:57:05 - Thread-131 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
column name : potential usage  
• "repo_name" (all tables that have it) : primary key to join information coming from different Github‐related tables.  
• "watch_count" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_REPOS) : approximate number of users “watching” the repository → watcher popularity measure.  
• "license" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LICENSES) : filter on approved OSS licenses (artistic‑2.0, isc, mit, apache‑2.0).  
• "path" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES) : file path; test for a “%.py” suffix to be sure the repository actually contains Python source.  
• "ref" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES) : keep only rows on the canonical branch ('refs/heads/master').  
• "id" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES / SAMPLE_CONTENTS) : internal object id, useful when verifying that a file really exists (only informative here).  
• "type" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022) : distinguishes “IssuesEvent”, “PullRequestEvent”, “ForkEvent”, etc.  We will count “IssuesEvent” and “ForkEvent”.  
• "created_at" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022) : epoch timestamp (micro‑seconds) of the event; restrict to April 2022 (‑‑between 2022‑04‑01 and 2022‑05‑01).  
• "public" (GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022) : be sure events are public (TRUE).  
• "watch_count", "forks", "issues" derived counts will be combined (forks*10 + issues*5 + watch_count, for instance) to pick the most active repository.  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each) that gradually explore the data and finally compute the requested ranking.  
All identifiers are put in double‑quotes as required.

```sql
--Description: 1) Quick look at the watch counts that are available.
SELECT 
    "repo_name",
    "watch_count"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_REPOS
ORDER BY "watch_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Inspect the list of licences we have in the LICENCES table.
SELECT DISTINCT 
    "license"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LICENSES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Confirm a few Python (.py) files that live on master branch.
SELECT 
    "repo_name",
    "path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE "ref" = 'refs/heads/master'
  AND "path" ILIKE '%.py'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Show how many Python files exist per repository (top 20).
SELECT 
    "repo_name",
    COUNT(*) AS "py_file_cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
WHERE "ref" = 'refs/heads/master'
  AND "path" ILIKE '%.py'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
ORDER BY "py_file_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Peek at the YEAR._2022 table to see event types in April 2022.
SELECT 
    "type",
    TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) AS "ts"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022
WHERE TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) BETWEEN '2022-04-01' AND '2022-05-01'
GROUP BY "type", TO_DATE(TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000))
ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Count public Issue events per repository for April 2022.
SELECT 
    "repo":"name"::STRING  AS "repo_name",
    COUNT(*)              AS "issue_event_cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022
WHERE "public" = TRUE
  AND "type" = 'IssuesEvent'
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) BETWEEN '2022-04-01' AND '2022-05-01'
GROUP BY "repo":"name"::STRING
ORDER BY "issue_event_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count public Fork events per repository for April 2022.
SELECT 
    "repo":"name"::STRING  AS "repo_name",
    COUNT(*)              AS "fork_event_cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022
WHERE "public" = TRUE
  AND "type" = 'ForkEvent'
  AND TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) BETWEEN '2022-04-01' AND '2022-05-01'
GROUP BY "repo":"name"::STRING
ORDER BY "fork_event_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Repositories that (a) have an accepted license and (b) at least one .py file.
SELECT DISTINCT l."repo_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LICENSES        l
JOIN GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES    f
  ON l."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
WHERE l."license" IN ('artistic-2.0', 'isc', 'mit', 'apache-2.0')
  AND f."ref" = 'refs/heads/master'
  AND f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Join watch counts with licence + Python filter to shortlist repos.
SELECT 
    r."repo_name",
    r."watch_count"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_REPOS    r
JOIN (
    SELECT DISTINCT l."repo_name"
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LICENSES l
    JOIN GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES f
      ON l."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
    WHERE l."license" IN ('artistic-2.0', 'isc', 'mit', 'apache-2.0')
      AND f."ref" = 'refs/heads/master'
      AND f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
) ok
  ON r."repo_name" = ok."repo_name"
ORDER BY r."watch_count" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final combined activity metric (watches + issues + forks) for April‑2022.
SELECT 
    base."repo_name",
    COALESCE(r."watch_count",0)                    AS "watch_cnt",
    COALESCE(iss."issue_event_cnt",0)              AS "issue_cnt",
    COALESCE(fk."fork_event_cnt",0)                AS "fork_cnt",
    (COALESCE(fk."fork_event_cnt",0)*10 +
     COALESCE(iss."issue_event_cnt",0)*5 +
     COALESCE(r."watch_count",0) )                 AS "activity_score"
FROM (
    SELECT DISTINCT l."repo_name"
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.LICENSES l
    JOIN GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES f
      ON l."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
    WHERE l."license" IN ('artistic-2.0', 'isc', 'mit', 'apache-2.0')
      AND f."ref" = 'refs/heads/master'
      AND f."path" ILIKE '%.py'
) base
LEFT JOIN GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_REPOS r
       ON base."repo_name" = r."repo_name"
LEFT JOIN (
    --Issue counts in April 2022
    SELECT 
        "repo":"name"::STRING AS "repo_name",
        COUNT(*)              AS "issue_event_cnt"
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022
    WHERE "public" = TRUE
      AND "type" = 'IssuesEvent'
      AND TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) BETWEEN '2022-04-01' AND '2022-05-01'
    GROUP BY "repo":"name"::STRING
) iss
       ON base."repo_name" = iss."repo_name"
LEFT JOIN (
    --Fork counts in April 2022
    SELECT 
        "repo":"name"::STRING AS "repo_name",
        COUNT(*)              AS "fork_event_cnt"
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2022
    WHERE "public" = TRUE
      AND "type" = 'ForkEvent'
      AND TO_TIMESTAMP("created_at"/1000000) BETWEEN '2022-04-01' AND '2022-05-01'
    GROUP BY "repo":"name"::STRING
) fk
       ON base."repo_name" = fk."repo_name"
ORDER BY "activity_score" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query surfaces the most active Python repositories in April 2022 while honouring the licence filter and combining watcher, issue, and fork signals; the top row returned is the candidate “most active” repository.
